Final answer: ### 1. Task outcome (short version):
Screening completed. 50 candidate studies assessed. 25 included, 25 excluded. All RCTs evaluating interventions for IUC 
insertion-related pain with self-reported pain outcomes were included; non-RCTs, reviews, methods articles, and 
irrelevant populations were excluded.

### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):
Inclusion criteria: RCTs evaluating an intervention for preventing IUC insertion-related pain, with comparison to 
placebo, no intervention, or active intervention, and primary outcomes of self-reported pain at tenaculum placement, 
during insertion, or after insertion (up to 6h). 
After careful review of each title and abstract, 25 studies met these criteria. They include pharmacological 
interventions (NSAIDs, local anesthetics, misoprostol, tramadol, nitric oxide donors) and non-pharmacological (lavender 
inhalation, bladder distension). All were RCTs with appropriate comparisons and pain measurements.
25 studies were excluded: not randomized (24, 27, 35, 37, 40), not original research (28 cohort, 29 qualitative, 30 
review, 31/36 GRADE guidelines, 32 committee opinion, 33 review, 34 review, 38 review, 39 systematic review, 41 review, 
42 meta-analysis, 44 survey, 45 methods, 46 opinion, 49 technique description, 50 review), wrong population/procedure 
(43 surgical abortion), or intervention for post-insertion treatment rather than prevention (47).
